    "body": "I found my issue for this and it's because of my terminal. I was testing on my Mac and also remotely on a RHEL8.5 box. When I actually sat in front of the RHEL box, it was rendering as expected. So I focused on my default terminal settings in the Mac. It looks like the issue is related to the \"Display ANSI colors\" settings. When I uncheck it, the text is just green and a shade of green. But keeping it selected only displays the 16 colors in the default palette. Those default ANSI colors are changeable though. So within my terminal settings, I changed a color I won't use for a style, like black, and set it to the hex values I wanted. Then I set my style to `(bold black)` within `starship.toml` and it worked as expected. \r\n<img width=\"663\" alt=\"settings\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/5083152/153697517-e9013d4d-ddda-470f-8cfe-78fe5cb69c4b.png\">\r\n<img width=\"410\" alt=\"term\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/5083152/153697519-c018fb0e-3fa5-4074-a998-2c7899019214.png\">\r\n",
